cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Plasmid Eco-Evo — Educational ecology and evolution of plasmids
  and mobile DNA
message: >-
  If you use or adapt this material, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Wongsatit
    given-names: Thanakrit
    alias: Austin
    email: austinwongsatit@kaist.ac.kr
abstract: >-
  An educational collection of biological case studies, conceptual
  frameworks, quantitative models and teaching figures on the ecology
  and evolution of plasmids and mobile DNA. It treats plasmids not
  only as molecular vectors but as evolving ecological entities whose
  persistence depends jointly on replication, host physiology,
  horizontal transmission, ecological interactions, environmental
  context and evolutionary history. Material derives only from
  published literature and independent teaching examples; every
  reference has a resolving DOI whose metadata has been checked.
keywords:
  - plasmid biology
  - horizontal gene transfer
  - mobile genetic elements
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - evolutionary ecology
  - science education
